## Vitamin D — Evidence Summary

The NHS states that vitamin D "helps regulate the amount of calcium and phosphate in the body," and that these nutrients are needed to keep bones, teeth and muscles healthy (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-d). The NHS medicines page for colecalciferol further states that this form of vitamin D "helps your body to take in more calcium and phosphorus from the food you eat" (https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/colecalciferol/about-colecalciferol). South Tees Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust states that vitamin D "exerts an effect primarily on calcium metabolism" and that "vitamin D receptors have been found on many different cell and tissues" (https://www.southtees.nhs.uk/services/pathology/tests/vitamin-d).

The NHS lists oily fish (such as salmon, sardines and mackerel), egg yolks, and fortified foods such as some fat spreads and breakfast cereals as food sources of vitamin D (https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/bone-health/food-for-strong-bones).

**Regarding the question about how much vitamin D adults need each day in the UK:** this service records and cites sources rather than advising, but the relevant sourced figures are as follows. The NHS states that the Department of Health and Social Care recommends that adults and children over 4 take a daily supplement containing 10 micrograms of vitamin D (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-d). NHS Cornwall and Isles of Scilly states that everyone over the age of 1 year should have 10 micrograms (400 IU) of vitamin D per day (https://cios.icb.nhs.uk/health/nutrition/vitamin-d). NICE guidance PH56 notes an RNI of 10 micrograms per day for everyone aged 4 and older, and also states that currently there is no reference nutrient intake for people aged between 4 and 65, reflecting differing framings within official guidance (https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ph56/chapter/Glossary). The NHS states that taking more than 100 micrograms of vitamin D a day could be harmful (https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/keeping-well/pregnancy-vitamins-and-supplements).

