The BNF lists calcium carbonate as a licensed medicine in the UK, with indications including phosphate binding in renal failure and hyperphosphataemia. NHS local formularies classify calcium supplements under section 09.05.01.01, indicating they are available both as prescription medicines and, in standard doses, as over-the-counter products.

