The NHS states that adults need 200 micrograms of folate a day (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-b). Regarding regulatory status, the Bedfordshire and Luton Joint Formulary records the 400 microgram tablet as available for self-care for routine supplementation in pregnancy, while the Cambridgeshire and Peterborough Formulary states that the 5 mg strength must be prescribed (https://www.cambridgeshireandpeterboroughformulary.nhs.uk/chaptersSubDetails.asp?FormularySectionID=9&SubSectionRef=09&SubSectionID=A100).

